  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Synthesis of Earthquake and Landslide Risk to Inform Emergency Preparedness and 
Planning in Nepal</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This is a study towards synthesising lessons about the nature, distribution, 
and evolution of risks from earthquake- and monsoon-triggered hazards (landslides and floods) in Nepal &#x2013; based on current literature and stakeholder consultations. This study would aim to shape recommendations for FCDO&#x2019;s support to the Government of Nepal, especially the implementation of the Resilience, Adaptation and Inclusion in Nepal and the Local Infrastructure Services Programme programmes, alongside advice to the Humanitarian Country Team of British Embassy Kathmandu to inform national-scale contingency planning.</narrative>
  </description>
